From 6e872ae37454ccebc8c5366c389716922ff215ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 06:22:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Apply the brand palette across the site

Replaces the placeholder ivory/sage palette with the studio's own colours:
green #2DBC9A, blue #465862, grey #F8F8F8, muted #A8AAAB. Every colour still
lives in one @theme block, so this is a token swap rather than a rewrite.

The footer moves from a dark band to #F8F8F8 as the palette specifies, which
changes it from light-on-dark to dark-on-light throughout.

Two supplied pairings fall below the 4.5:1 contrast floor for body text:
muted grey on the grey footer is 2.20:1, and white on the green is 2.39:1.
The VARIANT block at the top of globals.css holds the three values that
differ between using the hexes literally and using darker shades of the same
hues for small text. Currently set to the accessible variant pending a
decision; switching is a three-line edit.

Green becomes the primary action colour, blue the ink and the dark bands.
The palette has no danger colour, so one muted red is added for form errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
