From 6fe145b3da701d1da725f07c955b1cc39eabc13c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 06:31:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Finish the palette rollout and fix what the swap exposed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sweeping all 21 pages after the token swap turned up four things the
mechanical rename could not have caught:

- "Pending" states inherited the green tint, so an enquiry waiting on the
  studio looked like a confirmed one. Pending now wears amber, and the
  "confirm your email" and "not yet written" notices go with it — those are
  warnings, not confirmations.
- The green is too dark to read on the blue band (3.10:1), so eyebrow text
  and the large numerals there use a lighter tint of it instead.
- The sidebar's secondary text was a dark grey chosen when that panel was
  near-black; on the new blue it measured 1.53:1. It now uses a light grey
  that clears 4.5:1 there.
- The alert red sat at 4.27:1 on its own tint, just under the floor, and is
  now slightly darker.

All 29 tests still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L1bxKChEbqvtmDsqed6PxW
